## What Is Explicitly Out of Scope

Do not build any of the following, even if a reviewer suggests it:

| Item | Why Not |
|------|---------|
| In-page signup / login form | Auth UI lives in the Specview app |
| Stripe.js or Stripe Elements | Stripe-hosted checkout handles PCI scope; no SDK needed on the landing page |
| Annual pricing toggle | Monthly only for v1 |
| Team / Enterprise tier | Free + Pro only; revisit on inbound enterprise interest |
| Logged-in state detection (CTA swap to "Open app") | Would require a JS call to Specview on every page load — static posture is non-negotiable |
| Usage dashboard or project-counter UI | Belongs in the Specview app |
| A/B testing infrastructure | Ship one version; optimise when conversion data exists |
| Analytics pixel / tag | Out of scope for this epic |
| New CSS files or new font `<link>` tags | All tokens already loaded; adding weight would regress Lighthouse |
| `data-*` attribute registry or CTA component system | P4 — two anchors do not justify an abstraction layer |

